  "solution": "**Given:**\n\n 2x + (2)/(x) = 3 \n\n**Formula Used:**\n\n (x + (1)/(x))² = x² + (1)/(x²) + 2 \n\n**Calculation:**\n\n⇒ 2x + (2)/(x) = 3 \n\n⇒ x + (1)/(x) = (3)/(2) \n\n⇒ (x + (1)/(x))² = ((3)/(2))² \n\n⇒ x² + (1)/(x²) + 2 = (9)/(4) \n\n⇒ x² + (1)/(x²) = (9)/(4) - 2 \n\n⇒ x² + (1)/(x²) = (1)/(4) \n\n**∴ The correct answer is 1/4.**",
